# Copy this file into EACH app repo as `.dockerignore` (next to package.json).
# It keeps junk out of the build context → smaller, faster, safer images.
# The single most important line is `.env` — never bake secrets into an image.
#
# Patterns match from the context ROOT. `*.md` matches only root-level files;
# `**/*.md` matches at any depth. (Measured 29.9 on the backend image: with
# `*.md` alone it still carried docs/*.md and the test files.)
#
# The same file serves all three repos, so some lines are no-ops in a given
# one (a Vite app has no jest config; that is fine).

# Secrets and anything that could carry one. `.env.example` is the documented
# template and is allowed back in.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
secrets
**/*.log

# Version control, editor and Docker's own files
.git
.github
.gitignore
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.vscode
.idea

# Build outputs and dependencies — the image installs its own
node_modules
npm-debug.log
coverage
dist
build

# Documentation
**/*.md

# Tests and test/lint tooling — never needed at runtime
**/*.test.js
**/*.int.test.js
**/test
jest.config.*
jest.*.js
jest.*.cjs
.babelrc
.eslintrc*
.prettierrc*
nodemon.json
e2e
playwright-report
test-results
